    "description": "CertificateGateway is a legacy production class used during service admission. It calls its own protected, non-final currentTimeMillis method to obtain the current instant and then decides whether a certificate is expired. The method is not an injected dependency and is invoked internally rather than supplied by the caller. The deployment has frozen the production source, so adding a constructor parameter, a clock field, or another test hook is not permitted. Existing tests can construct CertificateGateway without any external service, but they cannot reliably test the expiry boundary because the result changes with wall-clock time. The team needs a deterministic test that fixes the instant, exercises both sides of the expiry threshold, and confirms the admission result without changing release behavior. The key decision is how to establish a controllable time boundary around the inherited call while honoring the prohibition on production-source changes.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide how tests can control the internally invoked clock when production code cannot be altered to expose an injection point.",
    "notes": "Test-specific-subclass fits because the frozen legacy class exposes its clock through a protected non-final method that tests can override without production-source changes; humble-object is the only same-family sibling."
  },
